      "username": "Kestrel",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/kestrel/{size}/802_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-05-03T02:59:23.511Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I GMed my first session of Sentinels last night with my normal game group and one of the players wanted to do something I wasn’t quite sure how to handle. They were in a group of about 4 minions and 3 villains and they wanted to taunt or provoke all of the minions to get them to focus on him rather than anyone else, kind of akin to taunts or marks in D&amp;D.</p>\n<p>Was that considered an attack? An overcome? A hinder to the minions? Do we just roleplay the taunt? We all kind of collectively hemmed and hawed about it and eventually settled on it being an overcome, but we could have made an argument for any of those things.</p>\n<p>How would you have handled it?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-05-03T02:59:23.511Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
